      "message": "btw. AFAICT this value was \u0027wrong\u0027 (in the sense of arbitrary) to begin with...\n\nA max size IPv4 packet is 65535 bytes (16-bit pkt length field), after conversion to/from ipv6 it increases by MTU_DELTA of 28 (- 20 bytes of ipv4 header + 40 bytes of ipv6 header + potential extra 8 byte ipv6 fragmentation header).\n\nThus the \u0027max\u0027 ipv6 L3 mtu (which is the one this is measuring) is actually 65535 + 28 \u003d 65563\n\nThe maximum non jumbogram ipv6 packet is 40 + 65535 \u003d 65575 bytes,\nso 65563 is smaller than that.\n\nThus 65563 is the value this *probably* should have been before,\nassuming the intent was to actually support the max possible size.\n\nHowever, none of this makes real sense, see commit message of this change.",
